The structure of ${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/algebraic-data-type.td")}s - sum because variants combine via "or" (one of mt or node), product because each variant's fields combine via "and" (a node has v and l and r).

The structure of ${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/algebraic-data-type.td")}s - **sum** because variants combine via "or" (one of `mt` or `node`), **product** because each variant's fields combine via "and" (a `node` has `v` and `l` and `r`).
